# Trials C and D — BLOCKED, and this file does not load.
#
# C would be: Interworking internet=0 plus an Apple Device IE in its
# internet-capable form. D would be both set. Both need a line like
#
#   vendor_elements=dd0800a0400000028022
#
# and that is exactly the line we must not write yet. hostapd's
# vendor_elements inserts whatever bytes it is given into beacons and probe
# responses without checking them; Apple's public material (WWDC17 session 717,
# 33:25) says the Apple Device IE carries internet state but does not publish
# its layout. The bit names in recon/ieaudit/apple.go come from third-party
# copies of an Apple header and from open-source head-unit projects, which is
# enough to decode a capture and argue about it, and not enough to transmit.
#
# A guessed IE produces a trial that cannot be interpreted either way: the phone
# ignoring it proves nothing if the bytes were wrong, and the phone reacting to
# it proves nothing about which field did the work.
#
# Unblocking condition (docs/ap-signalling.md, gate 3): a capture from a real
# internet-capable wireless CarPlay head unit, in both its internet-on and
# internet-off states, decoded by `ieaudit pcap` and showing which octets
# change. The F32 is not that reference — it transmits no Apple Device IE at
# all (docs/test-log.md, 2026-11-02).
#
# Rename to C-apple-ie.conf only after that capture exists and the bytes below
# are derived from it rather than from a flag-name table.
